@node Install, Connect, Getting Started, Getting Started
@section Installing Lyntin

Installing Lyntin is very easy.  Currently, Lyntin only runs under Unix,
but this should change very soon.

@enumerate
@item
Install python 1.3 or greater.
@item
unzip and untar lyntin; this will result in a directory named 'lt'.
@item
set the environment variable LYNTINDIR to be the name of the directory
you just created.
@item
modify/set the environment variable PYTHONPATH to include the name of
the directory you just created.
@item
mv the file 'direc_you_just_created/lt', eg lt/lt to a directory in
your path.
@item
type 'lt', and you're running lyntin.
@end enumerate

lyntin accepts command line arguments, and interprets them as files
filled with aliases/actions/subs/vars/gags


